t to get in bed and get a good number  of hours sleep every night between now  and the exams no staying up all night  revising regards do you think it's going  to help it will probably do more harm  than good take a good care of yourself  get enough sleep I have a good diet make  sure you get some exercise now is the  most important time actually to do  exercise so if you play football go and  play with some friends if you go to the  gym go there just it's so important to  vent off some stress and some steam  about these exams because you can get so  wound up in it that you lose perspective  so take good care of yourself because no  one's going to do this exam but you and  you've got to be in the best condition  possible in order to do your best the  last point that I want to make in this  video is discipline it's kind of Now or  Never when it comes to your exams you  have four or five weeks left until you  sit down an example and write things on  a piece of paper and few weeks after  that you're going to be graded based on  what you said now there's no way that  you can affect the outcome of that grade  after you taking the exam the only way  you're going to improve it is by working  before the exam in other words between  now and four or five weeks time now is  when it really counts and now is when  you've got a really knuckle down to it  and it sucks revision is not really the  most enjoyable thing to do in the world  but now is the only opportunity you're  going to have to  have an impact on a grade which is going  to stay with you for the next few years  and impact the rest of your educational  trajectory so knuckle down to it you've  got to be disciplined about it work hard  now and you'll be rewarded in the future  so you've got just over a month left  into your exams so it's time to get down  to it do lots and lots of practice  work hard take good care of yourself and  you are going to seriously thank  yourself for doing that in the future  next week we're g